gap_review_brief:
ROLE: Hit-feel and performance reviewer for Milestone 2, phase 3, package C. This is review only: change no tracked file. Work in /Users/arachne/repos/beat-em-up-PoC/.worktrees/m2-review-hit. It is detached at c27afaf (m2/hit-feel) and already imported, so cd there for every command. Everything you write, including any probe bot (.gd and .tscn files), goes under captures/review_hit/. The machine is shared: run one Godot process at a time and never leave one running. Record with Movie Maker directly, NEVER with tools/capture_combos.sh. The movies come out at 1600x900 even with --resolution 1280x720, so crop in those pixels. LOOK at every sheet with the Read tool, and judge from the frames, not from the code.

CONTEXT. Phase 3 is three changes:
- the localized white flash: HumanoidRig.flash_at() as a per-rig next_pass overlay, the "Hit flash" group in Hit feel, and a blocked hit flashing the defender at CombatActor.BLOCK_FLASH_AMOUNT 0.45;
- package A, the ragdoll: the push at the contact point with spin caps, staggers at 0.9 influence, and KO bodies that lie, blink off and vanish while dummies blink back in at their post;
- package B, the grab: the hold view and the waist bend.

The code, ragdoll and grab lenses are already done. Don't re-report their findings; cite them by id if you see them:
- code-01: the flash sits at the raw contact point, so a thrown pipe shows none, a body impact shows a faint one, and a body already staggering flashes the wrong part;
- code-02: a respawn can come back inside a lying body;
- code-03: the lens bobs on every grab and release;
- ragdoll-01: the throw pops upright and skates;
- ragdoll-02: the hook stagger doesn't read from the side;
- ragdoll-03: the side-view health bar sits on the head;
- grab-01 to grab-08, including grab-03 (the combat log over the knee, a spec question) and grab-05 (the knee's flash whitens 16% of the view).

APPROVED, so not defects:
- heavy-tier knockdowns get the full ragdoll;
- staggers at 0.9 influence;
- KO bodies blink off and vanish, and dummies blink back in at their post, or beside it if it is occupied, with no hits or grabs during the blink-in;
- KO bodies take no hits;
- the push at the contact point with spin caps;
- the localized flash;
- the grab view pans down, with the lens moving back and up while holding;
- the knee rises a little to the right;
- the throw ends in the stance;
- the victim stands 6 cm closer;
- phase 1's eight defaults (HANDOFF Decisions log).

OPEN WITH GAME-BOY: report what you see, and change nothing:
- more contortion on the contact push;
- the grab's lens pull-back and the bend's depth;
- the combat log over the knee;
- a minimum on-screen size for the side-view flash.

PART A, HIT FEEL (required). The bot scripts' headers and act tables list every act (tests/bot/combo_bot.gd and tests/bot/vfx_bot.gd).
1. Record all 34 combo_bot acts in one run:
   `godot --path . --write-movie captures/review_hit/combo.avi --fixed-fps 60 --resolution 1280x720 res://tests/bot/combo_bot.tscn > captures/review_hit/combo.log 2>&1`
   Record all 22 vfx_bot acts the same way into vfx.avi and vfx.log. The logs print '=== <title>' for each act and 'f<N> <victim>: <move> <dmg> <TIER>' for each hit. With Movie Maker writing one frame per tick, movie time is about N/60 s; confirm the offset against the caption on a sheet. combo_bot gives dummies 500 HP, so it has no KOs.
2. No bot shows the thrown pipe in side view. Write a probe bot, captures/review_hit/probe_bot.gd extending res://tests/bot/combo_bot.gd and overriding _run with its own act list, the way the grab reviewer did in /Users/arachne/repos/beat-em-up-PoC/.worktrees/m2-review-grab/captures/review_grab/probe_bot.gd. Give it two acts: (i) 'Pipe: pick up, 3 swings, throw' with cam &"side_view"; (ii) the spin kick on three dummies at low health (max_health about 10), in both views, so three KOs, blink-offs and respawns happen at once.
3. Judge each tier (LIGHT, HEAVY, FINISHER, taken from the log) in each view where an act exists:
   - Does the hit read? Look at the flash, burst, word, shake, impact frame and push together.
   - Does the localized flash show on the struck part?
   - Does any effect fill the first-person view? Give the share of the view, as a %.
   Cover these in particular:
   - the heavy-tier knockdowns: flying kick, spin kick and back elbow in both views, and the thrown pipe;
   - three flashes at once on the spin kick;
   - the stomp under the view;
   - 'VFX: P P P P, impact frame off';
   - the haymaker's spit and tooth;
   - the parry spark with the cyan whole-body flash next to the white localized flash;
   - the tier sizes side by side.
4. Give a verdict with evidence (capture, time or frame) for each 10:55 known item:
   - (a) A hit on the player shows no first-person flash. Does it still read (shake, HUD)? Look at the clean jab after the guard is let go in 'Guard break', at 'Flank hit lands', and at their side views. Also check the blocked-hit flash (0.45) on the player's own guard arms in 'Block: sparring jab from the front': readable, or glare?
   - (b) Does the side-view flash hide under the burst? Check P P P P, K K K, the haymaker and the tier sizes in side view. Report only; Game-boy's default is to leave it.
   - (d) Measure the light burst's share of the view at jab range (VFX P P P P; tier sizes at 1.4 m).
   - (e) Is the bruised look subtle in side view? Check 'VFX: damage looks (side view)' and 'VFX: damage looks held (side view)'. Also check whether the localized flash still covers the bloodied look on the held act's jab. The act's comment and tests/test_vfx.gd test_hit_flash_still_covers_the_damage_look both assume it does.
   - (f) What does the always-on combat log hide in each side-view act? Tie the verdict to grab-03's proposal.
   - (g) Do the speed lines repeat? Record 'VFX: P P P P, light to finisher' twice and compare the finisher's frames (ffmpeg framemd5, or a difference blend). Do the same with combo_bot 'P P P P (side view)' twice. Note that vfx_director.gd:76 calls rng.randomize() and only vfx_bot reseeds (vfx_bot.gd:73). combo_bot and ragdoll_bot don't, yet speed_lines.gd:26-27 says 'the bots do'.
   - (c) is in Part B.

PART B, PERFORMANCE (required, bounded). Movie Maker can't show a dropped frame, so run in real time, windowed, without --write-movie. Use a probe bot in captures/review_hit/ that logs, for every rendered frame:
- the frame delta (Time.get_ticks_usec() in _process);
- Performance TIME_PROCESS and TIME_PHYSICS_PROCESS;
- RENDER_TOTAL_DRAW_CALLS_IN_FRAME;
- the pipeline-compilation monitors (Performance PIPELINE_COMPILATIONS_*; check the names with `godot --headless --doctool <scratch dir>`);
- the viewport's measured render times (RenderingServer.viewport_set_measure_render_time, then viewport_get_measured_render_time_cpu and viewport_get_measured_render_time_gpu).
Other agents record on this machine, so repeat each case 3 times and report the median and the max. Trust compile counts and draw calls over milliseconds.
Measure:
1. The first contact flash of a fresh process, in first person and in side view, against later hits. Did pipelines compile on the hit frame? The code reviewer left open whether _warm_flash compiles anything (humanoid_rig.gd:458-470). It puts a BoxMesh at the feet of the first rig built, which is the player's, so in first person the box is outside the view, and the box is not skinned. Its own doc measured 4-12 ms extra on the first hit without the warm-up.
2. The first finisher of a run against the second (known item c): is the dropped frame still there, and what compiles on it?
3. Six ragdolls at once, with the contact push on and off (ragdoll_kick_at_contact). The room has 3 dummies; add 3 as WP4's probe did (/Users/arachne/repos/beat-em-up-PoC/.worktrees/m2-ragdoll/captures/review_mech/probe_perf.gd). Compare against WP4's 0.6 ms of physics and HANDOFF's 1.2-1.5 ms.
4. The flash overlay's cost: draw calls and frame time with three bodies flashing against none.
5. A spike, if any, on the KO vanish frame and the respawn blink-in frame.
A perf finding needs a frame over 16.7 ms, or a repeatable compile on a gameplay frame.

PART C (only if headroom remains), mechanics probes with a capture each:
- the player KO'd while holding (the hold view and the held victim);
- a contact push or a throw into the curb or a wall (limbs through the geometry);
- a respawn beside an occupied post, captured on video.

RETURN:
- Findings, each with: id (hit-NN or perf-NN), lens, title, severity, evidence (capture path and time or frame, log line), repro steps, suggested fix, and the files a fix touches.
- One verdict line for each of the seven known items (a) to (g).
- The list of acts checked, with their views.
- An explicit list of what you did not get to.
Spec questions go to the lead and stay out of fixes.
